	(footprint "lc:SW_Omron_D2MQ-1-TR"
		(layer "F.Cu")
		(uuid "cf020b7d-05d8-4617-bc54-d96d392e01ad")
		(at 104.5 115.95)
		(descr "Omron D2MQ-1-TR ultra-slim snap-action switch, right-angled PCB terminals, pin plunger, lying flat (2.7 mm tall), plunger toward -Y. Checked against the Omron D2MQ datasheet (Terminals/Appearances, PCB terminals right-angled; Dimensions, pin plunger): body 8.2 x 6.5 (6.08 past the step), terminal tails 2.5 mm pitch, 1.2 mm behind the body end, blade 0.8 wide with 1.3 mm barbs; Omron recommends 1.6 mm round holes. Pin plunger d0.8 in line with the left body mounting hole (x -2.0), hole centres 1.6 mm from the terminal end, OP 5.7+/-0.2 and FP <= 6.1 from the hole centre line (y -8.5 / -8.9 here). Tails are 1.5 mm long: they stick 0.7 mm out of a 0.8 mm board, trim flush. Pad 1 = middle terminal (NO); both ends = pad 2 = GND.")
